"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nI visited the main branch of Sinchang Gukbap, one of the famous pork rice soup restaurants in Busan.  \nI went to check it out after it was introduced on Michin Matjib (Crazy Good Restaurants).  \n\nSince I visited during a late lunch hour on a weekday, luckily I could enter immediately without a wait.  \n\nPerhaps because we looked like tourists from out of town, they guided us to a seat where famous people had sat.  \nActually, those things aren't very important to us, but since there were plenty of seats anyway, we sat in a spot where a celebrity had been.  \n\nCute enough, each chair had the name of who sat there.  \nI sat in the seat where Chairman Lee Jae-yong had sat.  \n\nThere were many celebrities' signatures on the walls.  \n\nThe pork rice soup I ordered came out quickly.  \nI ordered the standard toryeom (rinsed with hot broth) pork rice soup and ttaro-gukbap (rice and soup served separately), but since I eat everything well and have an unrefined palate, I didn't feel a big difference.  \nBoth were delicious.  \n\nIt was a clear, light style without being greasy.  \n\nIt's a style that might be polarizing, but I liked it.  \n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"